From 26f263eebbf0c074a3b4eec354f54642c7c785b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NexusGuide <NexusGuidem1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:56:08 +0330
Subject: [PATCH] fix: add the launcher icons the manifest has always
 referenced

The first CI build failed in :app:processDebugResources, before any
Kotlin was compiled: AndroidManifest.xml pointed at @mipmap/ic_launcher
and @mipmap/ic_launcher_round and the app had no mipmap directory at
all. Phase 4 shipped a manifest whose icons were never drawn.

Adds an adaptive icon for API 26+, a monochrome layer for themed icons
on API 33+, and PNGs at five densities, since minSdk is 24 and API
24-25 do not understand adaptive icons. The PNGs are rendered from the
same coordinates as the vector so the two cannot drift apart.

Two launch-theme bugs found alongside it:

values/ and values-night/ both defined launch_background as the same
navy, so a light-theme launch flashed dark before Compose painted
#F8FAFC. Each now matches its scheme's background in core/ui/Theme.kt.

values-night/themes.xml redefined Theme.Nexora without windowBackground,
so in dark mode the launch theme fell back to the Material light
background - the white flash the theme exists to prevent. Deleted, so
the one definition serves both.

Every @string/@color/@drawable/@mipmap/@xml reference in the manifest,
resources and Kotlin was audited against what is defined; nothing else
is missing.
